1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,503
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:07,590
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,844
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:13,012
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:19,519
[Cita] <i>Atoy appreciated</i>
<i>that you were there.</i>

7
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:21,271
<i>Especially now that he's</i>
<i>going through something.</i>

8
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:25,525
[Karla] I apologized because
he thinks we're honest with him, but…

9
00:00:25,608 --> 00:00:26,526
we're not.

10
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:29,154
[Gavin] <i>You really take after</i>
<i>your Brother Atoy, huh?</i>

11
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:30,447
You're hot-headed too.

12
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:33,450
[Ame] <i>Atoy wanted to see Janine.</i>

13
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:37,120
But he found out Janine
was already pulled out of school.

14
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:40,040
Tell her, if she doesn't
want to talk to me,

15
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:41,624
she shouldn't involve Janine.

16
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:43,251
[in English] After what you did
to my family?

17
00:00:43,334 --> 00:00:45,044
I know you're a good kid.

18
00:00:45,837 --> 00:00:48,798
You're just surrounded by liars.

19
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:50,341
You're the one who's pitiful!

20
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:51,968
There are more liars around you!

21
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:53,011
Why don't you ask Karla?!

22
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:54,888
- Karla?!
- No-- Nothing.

23
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:56,598
We're going to America?

24
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:59,809
It's okay with you
if you don't see your daddy anymore?

25
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:01,811
It's fine with me. He's bad anyway.

26
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:05,482
That damned husband of yours
used me as a shield,

27
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:06,608
that's why I got shot!

28
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:08,943
Dad, you don't need to say that.

29
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:10,195
[in English] You're being unfair to Red.

30
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:13,114
Who else are you looking for, besides Ame?

31
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:15,408
A-- Atoy.

32
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:17,202
[Faye] <i>Can we meet later?</i>

33
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:19,871
Ah, yes-- Okay. Where can we meet you?

34
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:21,998
Are you hiding something from me?

35
00:01:22,874 --> 00:01:24,918
I hope you won't be angry with us.

36
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:28,713
- Angry?
- Let your Brother Atoy rest.

37
00:01:28,797 --> 00:01:29,964
[Cita] <i>Karla, what was that?</i>

38
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:32,258
<i>Are you going to tell Atoy the truth?</i>

39
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:33,885
<i>Didn't I warn you?</i>

40
00:01:33,968 --> 00:01:37,055
We won't add to what
he's going through anymore.

41
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:41,476
[Atoy] <i>I'll never forget this scarf.</i>

42
00:01:41,559 --> 00:01:44,729
Why, of all men, did it have
to be my father, Godmother?

43
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:46,314
PREVIOUSLY

44
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:48,233
[music fades]

45
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:50,610
You're my godmother.

46
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:53,863
[Atoy] How--

47
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:58,409
- You were my mother's best friend.
- [Cita sobs softly]

48
00:02:00,286 --> 00:02:01,913
You deceived my mother before,

49
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:05,083
and now you're deceiving me every day,

50
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:06,918
whenever you see my face.

51
00:02:07,001 --> 00:02:08,837
How can you do that, Godmother?

52
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:10,839
How can you do that?

53
00:02:10,922 --> 00:02:11,881
Atoy…

54
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:15,552
Atoy, Atoy.

55
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:18,930
- [sobs]
- [pensive music playing]

56
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:20,223
So, Karla?

57
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:23,852
Is there something else I need to know?

58
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:28,148
Is there something else I need to know?

59
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,152
[sobbing]

60
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:37,115
[sobbing]

61
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:38,533
Okay, because…

62
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,368
I saw this…

63
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:45,165
I saw a picture of a child

64
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:47,333
being carried by Dad.

65
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:52,338
[sobbing]

66
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:53,798
[Atoy] I don't know if that's…

67
00:02:54,757 --> 00:02:56,759
I just have this feeling…

68
00:02:57,385 --> 00:02:58,928
or if my suspicion is right.

69
00:02:59,804 --> 00:03:01,472
So, Karla?

70
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:03,558
Is my suspicion right…

71
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:06,936
about who you are?

72
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:07,937
[sobs]

73
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:09,731
[Atoy] Huh?

74
00:03:09,814 --> 00:03:13,610
- [sobbing]
- [melancholic music playing]

75
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:15,987
Brother, that's what
I've been hiding from you.

76
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:18,114
[sobbing]

77
00:03:18,197 --> 00:03:20,283
Sir Delfin is my real father.

78
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:22,160
[sobbing]

79
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:24,787
I'm the product of their betrayal.

80
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:28,958
[sobbing]

81
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:31,502
Atoy-- Atoy, Atoy.

82
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:33,713
- [sobs]
- [Atoy chuckles] So…

83
00:03:35,673 --> 00:03:36,883
You've known for a long time?

84
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:41,304
No, brother. I only found out recently.

85
00:03:42,138 --> 00:03:43,264
Please believe me.

86
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:45,266
I've wanted to tell you for a long time,

87
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:46,726
but I've been having a hard time.

88
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:48,394
- A hard time?
- I was ashamed to tell you!

89
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:50,897
Ashamed? But you pretended?!

90
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:53,358
- Brother.
- [Atoy] How could you--

91
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:54,359
[Cita] Atoy.

92
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:55,360
No--

93
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:57,820
[smirks] I never fell short
in caring for you.

94
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:59,864
How could you do this to me?

95
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,741
[sobbing]

96
00:04:01,824 --> 00:04:04,702
I treated you like family!

97
00:04:04,786 --> 00:04:06,329
[Cita sobs]

98
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:10,041
- Huh?
- Atoy, Karla and I love you. [sobs]

99
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:12,835
I've long wanted to tell you
everything before,

100
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:16,798
but Delfin told me
to keep it secret from you.

101
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:17,757
[Atoy] To keep it secret?

102
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:19,842
Don't-- Don't use Dad

103
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:21,719
to justify what you did, Godmother!

104
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,681
You're still making
a fool of me up to now!

105
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:26,266
- Atoy, Atoy.
- [Atoy] What?!

106
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:30,019
I knew the day would come
when I'd tell you everything.

107
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:34,148
Ah-- Ah, forgive me, forgive me.

108
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:37,151
Blame me, not Karla.

109
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:39,654
I just didn't want to ruin what we had.

110
00:04:39,737 --> 00:04:41,656
I didn't want to hurt you, Atoy.

111
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:44,867
- Atoy, please forgive me.
- [Atoy] You're unbelievable.

112
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:47,578
- Unbelievable!
- [Cita] Atoy.

113
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:50,039
[Cita sobbing]

114
00:04:50,123 --> 00:04:51,207
Atoy.

115
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:53,418
[sobs] Atoy, please forgive me.

116
00:04:53,501 --> 00:04:54,419
Don't come near me.

117
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:56,921
[sobbing]

118
00:04:57,005 --> 00:05:00,466
- I don't need you.
- Atoy. [sobbing]

119
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:01,551
You too.

120
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:03,011
[sobbing]

121
00:05:03,094 --> 00:05:04,971
Atoy…

122
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:08,099
[sobs] Atoy, Atoy.

123
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:10,393
[door clicks shut]

124
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:13,187
[door lock clicking]

125
00:05:30,955 --> 00:05:36,085
[sobs]

126
00:05:38,838 --> 00:05:41,215
[thuds]

127
00:05:41,299 --> 00:05:47,930
[sobbing]

128
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:51,726
[sobbing]

129
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:57,982
[thuds]

130
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:04,322
[sobs]

131
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:07,075
[suave theme music playing]

132
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:11,370
[scratches]

133
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:12,955
[snipping]

134
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:14,874
[sewing machine clacking]

135
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:19,670
[gunshots]

136
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:24,509
[snipping]

137
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:26,469
[electronic blipping]

138
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:31,224
[music fades]

139
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:35,895
'Toy. 'Toy.

140
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:39,649
Are you serious?
You really don't need Miss Cita?

141
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:44,946
Bro…

142
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:49,033
I get it.

143
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:51,869
I get that feeling of betrayal.

144
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:55,081
It's like being punched
in the face when you found out.

145
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:56,124
[pensive music playing]

146
00:06:56,207 --> 00:06:57,500
But I think…

147
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:00,753
Miss Cita's regret

148
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:05,758
and concern for you are real.

149
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:08,928
Bro, of course,

150
00:07:09,011 --> 00:07:10,847
if I were in her position,

151
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:14,809
I wouldn't immediately admit to you
that I was with your dad.

152
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:17,437
Not because I didn't want to be caught,

153
00:07:18,312 --> 00:07:21,649
but because I wouldn't want to ruin…

154
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:24,569
ruin what we had, our bond,

155
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:25,862
our family.

156
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:28,531
Right? That's important. That's precious.

157
00:07:29,198 --> 00:07:31,742
It just makes me
more furious at my father.

158
00:07:33,953 --> 00:07:35,329
I can't stand seeing them.

159
00:07:38,082 --> 00:07:40,501
[in English] Okay. Okay, okay, okay, okay.

160
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:43,880
Fine, fine. Let it out.

161
00:07:43,963 --> 00:07:46,382
But don't hold onto it, bro.

162
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:51,304
No family is perfect, but…

163
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:53,556
You know…

164
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:58,436
They're the only ones
I see who truly love you.

165
00:07:58,519 --> 00:08:00,313
I saw it in Karla.

166
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:02,315
- Especially in Miss Cita.
- [Atoy] No!

167
00:08:02,398 --> 00:08:05,026
Ibyang is the only one who truly loves me!

168
00:08:05,109 --> 00:08:06,319
[music fades]

169
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:09,405
She's the only genuine person in my life.

170
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:12,909
[epic music playing]

171
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:24,545
[music fades]

172
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:30,885
Ma'am.

173
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:34,931
Can I speak with Boss Red now?

174
00:08:35,848 --> 00:08:37,350
He needs to know something.

175
00:08:37,975 --> 00:08:40,728
He's resting, Mongki. What do you want?

176
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:43,356
Roger called me.

177
00:08:44,148 --> 00:08:47,944
He's following Sister Norma
and her niece here in Manila.

178
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:49,570
[suspicious music playing]

179
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:50,821
[in English] Wait. Wait, what?

180
00:08:50,905 --> 00:08:52,114
[in English] So, it's confirmed?

181
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,866
Sister Norma is still alive?

182
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:57,828
Yes, ma'am. My man confirmed it.

183
00:08:57,912 --> 00:09:00,706
And he overheard they're meeting someone

184
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,708
to talk to Atoy.

185
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:05,044
[in English] Wait. [sighs]

186
00:09:05,127 --> 00:09:06,921
[in English] Why
are they looking for Atoy?

187
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:11,509
I don't know, ma'am.
That's all he heard from the conversation.

188
00:09:11,592 --> 00:09:14,512
But they said they'll meet
at Emery's Café.

189
00:09:15,263 --> 00:09:18,349
There, at the corner. Near the hospital.

190
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:21,477
We need to get ahead of that Atoy.

191
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:25,022
Sister Norma is the only one who knows
where Audrey's real child is.

192
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:29,569
This is the perfect opportunity
to get back at that nuisance, Atoy.

193
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:36,701
They said they're already here, Sis Ame?

194
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:39,704
Ah, I texted her niece.

195
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:43,291
She said they'll come straight here
after the hospital checkup.

196
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:50,006
Sis Ame, does this mean
I'll finally meet my real parents?

197
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:51,591
Yes.

198
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:53,551
[melancholic music playing]

199
00:09:53,634 --> 00:09:54,927
Oh? Aren't you happy?

200
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:59,307
It's fine, but…

201
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:02,476
I'm thinking of Master Grumpy.

202
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:06,564
If that happens, I'll probably leave him

203
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:09,233
if my parents want to take me.

204
00:10:10,401 --> 00:10:13,529
We'll think about that later.

205
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:16,490
Look, that looks delicious.
Let's order first.

206
00:10:16,574 --> 00:10:17,908
- Come on!
- Okay.

207
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:20,202
[music fades]

208
00:10:32,214 --> 00:10:34,759
[pensive music playing]

209
00:10:34,842 --> 00:10:37,219
[Atoy] <i>You're causing trouble.</i>
<i>You're even talking back to your mom.</i>

210
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:39,305
<i>What's wrong with you?</i>
<i>You're growing up backwards.</i>

211
00:10:39,388 --> 00:10:42,767
If I were your parent, I'd be angry too.

212
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:44,393
But Mom is like that too!

213
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:45,311
She hasn't changed!

214
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:46,604
What hasn't changed?

215
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:49,315
Godmother Cita is so decent.
What's the problem with your mother?

216
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,569
Nothing, brother. You wouldn't understand.

217
00:10:54,987 --> 00:10:57,198
How can I understand if you won't tell me?

218
00:11:00,242 --> 00:11:05,414
Karla, it's bad to hold grudges
against your parents.

219
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:06,415
Remember that.

220
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:09,126
Nothing good will come of it.

221
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:12,254
Believe me.

222
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:17,927
[melodramatic music playing]

223
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:23,349
[sobs]

224
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:40,324
Karla?

225
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:42,034
[sobs]

226
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:46,330
I've been trying to call you.

227
00:11:51,043 --> 00:11:51,961
[Karla] Why?

228
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:54,463
So you can insult Brother Atoy again?

229
00:11:56,465 --> 00:11:58,801
Fine, he's bad! Can you just leave?

230
00:11:58,884 --> 00:11:59,885
[Gavin] No, Karla.

231
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:02,263
I owe you an apology.

232
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:05,307
You told him that I'm a liar?

233
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:08,227
And that we're really siblings?

234
00:12:09,728 --> 00:12:11,063
Not everything.

235
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:14,191
I didn't mean to.
I just got really angry with him.

236
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:18,279
It's fine. It's over.

237
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:22,533
So, we don't have to lie to him anymore.

238
00:12:23,367 --> 00:12:24,618
He already knows?

239
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:41,844
[melancholic music playing]

240
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:45,473
[sobs] He's already angry with me and Mom.

241
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:50,769
What hurts more
is I already lost a father,

242
00:12:50,853 --> 00:12:53,689
and now I might lose a brother.

243
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:56,859
He's just angry now.

244
00:12:56,942 --> 00:12:58,694
But Brother Atoy loves you.

245
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:02,990
Especially you, Karla.

246
00:13:03,073 --> 00:13:04,325
[sentimental music playing]

247
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:07,453
Brother Atoy loves you very much.

248
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:09,580
[sobs]

249
00:13:10,706 --> 00:13:15,002
["In Nothing" by Wickermoss
with Neth Macam playing]

250
00:13:15,085 --> 00:13:21,717
♪ <i>Don't try to</i> ♪

251
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,011
♪ <i>Guess the future</i> ♪

252
00:13:24,094 --> 00:13:28,766
♪ <i>The cards you hold are from the past</i> ♪

253
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:31,310
[Cathy] Gavin!

254
00:13:37,399 --> 00:13:38,817
[in English] What's going on?

255
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:40,444
We're just talking.

256
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,489
Why are you two so close?

257
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:46,242
Are you really talking,

258
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:48,327
or is this girl flirting with you?

259
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:50,913
You're full of dirty thoughts.
We're not doing anything wrong.

260
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:53,874
- Stop flirting with my boyfriend.
- [Gavin] Cathy!

261
00:13:53,958 --> 00:13:56,168
Don't shout at Karla. I approached her.

262
00:13:56,252 --> 00:13:57,753
We were discussing something.

263
00:13:58,379 --> 00:14:00,172
[in English] Oh, really?

264
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:01,590
[in English] So, tell me.

265
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:04,009
What exactly were you talking about?

266
00:14:04,093 --> 00:14:06,971
Is it really that important
that you had to meet?

267
00:14:07,721 --> 00:14:10,724
[in English] It's personal!
None of your business.

268
00:14:10,808 --> 00:14:12,309
Really?

269
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:13,394
Just a reminder.

270
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:16,605
I'm your girlfriend, not her!

271
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:19,275
[in English] I'm the one that's supposed
to know everything!

272
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:20,776
[scoffs]

273
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:24,405
[melancholic music playing]

274
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:26,532
Go, follow her.

275
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:34,498
[melodramatic music playing]

276
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:50,890
- Take care.
- Mmm-mmm.

277
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:58,898
[ominous music playing]

278
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:01,108
Don't move.

279
00:15:02,109 --> 00:15:03,694
- Sir.
- Or you'll go straight to the morgue.

280
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:06,280
Sir, we don't have any money.

281
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:08,198
Behave yourselves.

282
00:15:15,205 --> 00:15:18,125
[tense music playing]

283
00:15:23,464 --> 00:15:24,673
[in English] Hello, Sister Norma.

284
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,091
[in English] Remember me?

285
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:27,760
[music swells]

286
00:15:27,843 --> 00:15:31,138
[in English] Her mother
is in a coma and, um…

287
00:15:31,221 --> 00:15:32,848
she might not wake up.

288
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:37,561
So, I'm entrusting the child to you.

289
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,104
- Sister Norma! Sister Norma.
- [nun, in English] Excuse me?!

290
00:15:39,188 --> 00:15:40,064
- [Red] Uh…
- [nun] Excuse me!

291
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:41,273
Wait! Eight years ago,

292
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:45,235
there was a two-month-old baby
my wife, Martina, gave you.

293
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:48,113
Ma-- Martina Regalia is her name.
Do you remember?

294
00:15:48,197 --> 00:15:49,990
Sister, do you still remember me?

295
00:15:50,074 --> 00:15:51,575
We just want to find the child.

296
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:53,035
We want to know who adopted her.

297
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:55,871
[Martina] You're good at hiding.

298
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:58,540
[in English] But finally, you're here.

299
00:15:59,541 --> 00:16:01,418
Come with us calmly,

300
00:16:01,502 --> 00:16:03,295
so there won't be any problems.

301
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:04,463
[in English] Okay?

302
00:16:05,255 --> 00:16:07,383
[whimpers]

303
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:09,927
[Norma wailing]

304
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,470
[Faye] Let us go, sir!

305
00:16:11,553 --> 00:16:12,805
[Norma wailing]

306
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:14,014
[Faye] Auntie.

307
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:18,519
[wailing]

308
00:16:18,602 --> 00:16:20,562
- Sir!
- [wails]

309
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:21,647
[Mongki] Kneel, kneel!

310
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:28,362
[both whimpering]

311
00:16:28,445 --> 00:16:30,614
[Martina, in English] Shut it!

312
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,826
- The child I gave for adoption…
- [sobbing]

313
00:16:33,909 --> 00:16:35,035
Where is she?

314
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:38,706
- [whimpering]
- [music fades]

315
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:41,458
- [sobbing]
- [ominous music playing]

316
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:44,044
I won't--

317
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:48,424
I won't tell you!

318
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:54,221
You're-- You're evil!

319
00:16:54,304 --> 00:16:55,931
- [dramatic sting]
- [sobbing]

320
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,224
So, what do we do?

321
00:16:57,307 --> 00:16:58,350
Should we just kill your companion?!

322
00:16:58,434 --> 00:16:59,643
- Have mercy, sir!
- [whimpering]

323
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:00,644
[sobbing]

324
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:03,564
- Please, have mercy!
- [wailing]

325
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:05,607
Auntie…

326
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:07,192
[wailing]

327
00:17:07,276 --> 00:17:10,154
[Martina] That poor companion of yours!

328
00:17:10,237 --> 00:17:11,947
She'll get dragged into this.

329
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:15,451
You're stammering.
You're so hard to talk to.

330
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:17,411
[both whimpering]

331
00:17:17,494 --> 00:17:19,121
You still won't say anything?

332
00:17:19,204 --> 00:17:23,459
[whimpering]

333
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:29,256
The child… Where is she?

334
00:17:29,339 --> 00:17:35,137
[whimpering and sobbing]

335
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:42,102
- [sobbing]
- She's with…

336
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:48,317
Ame, Ibyang!

337
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,735
- [tense music playing]
- [whimpering]

338
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:51,111
Ame?

339
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:52,279
Ibyang?

340
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:56,492
[whimpering, quivering]

341
00:17:57,576 --> 00:18:00,412
Ame is the one…

342
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:01,789
The one from the orphanage.

343
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:02,998
[sobs]

344
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,917
She's the one who took in Ibyang,

345
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,044
the child you've been searching for.

346
00:18:07,127 --> 00:18:09,630
[whimpering, quivering]

347
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:12,883
[in English] I've…
I've heard that name before.

348
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:15,010
[sobbing]

349
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:16,678
Please let us go.

350
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:18,055
[whimpering]

351
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:19,640
- [phone ringing]
- [squeals]

352
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:21,350
[gasping, whimpering]

353
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:22,476
[Faye, in English] Auntie. Auntie.

354
00:18:22,559 --> 00:18:26,063
- [tense music playing]
- [phone ringing]

355
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:29,399
[whimpering, quivering]

356
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:30,359
[Ame on the phone] <i>Hello?</i>

357
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:33,320
We're already here at Emery's Café.

358
00:18:33,403 --> 00:18:35,864
Where are you and Sister Norma?

359
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:39,159
I brought Ibyang too,
because she wanted to see Sister.

360
00:18:41,912 --> 00:18:44,915
[line beeping]

361
00:18:44,998 --> 00:18:46,667
The call dropped.

362
00:18:49,253 --> 00:18:50,420
SORRY, PHONE'S BATTERY IS LOW

363
00:18:50,504 --> 00:18:51,672
I'M ON THE WAY THERE
HOW WILL I RECOGNIZE YOU?

364
00:18:56,176 --> 00:18:57,636
SORRY, PHONE'S BATTERY IS LOW

365
00:18:57,719 --> 00:18:58,887
I'M ON THE WAY THERE
HOW WILL I RECOGNIZE YOU?

366
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:02,224
[Ame] I'm the one in the green T-shirt,

367
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:04,768
the smallest one.

368
00:19:08,939 --> 00:19:12,401
I'M THE ONE IN THE GREEN T-SHIRT
THE SMALLEST ONE

369
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:17,865
[Faye and Norma whimpering, quivering]

370
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:20,284
Now, you two,

371
00:19:20,367 --> 00:19:23,495
- I better not see you anywhere near Atoy,
- [Faye] Yes.

372
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:24,746
Ame, or Ibyang.

373
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:26,665
[Faye] Yes. Yes, ma'am.

374
00:19:26,748 --> 00:19:30,252
[in English] Consider this
a second chance at life.

375
00:19:30,335 --> 00:19:34,298
Because if I find out you're still
in Manila, there won't be a third.

376
00:19:34,381 --> 00:19:35,507
[in English] Do you understand me?

377
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:38,135
Yes, ma'am. [whimpers]

378
00:19:38,218 --> 00:19:39,845
[pensive music playing]

379
00:19:39,928 --> 00:19:41,471
You understand, right?

380
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:45,058
If it were just me, you'd already be dead!

381
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:47,811
Yes, yes! [whimpering, quivering]

382
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:49,938
- Please have mercy on us.
- You handle these two.

383
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:53,025
[whimpers] Auntie.

384
00:19:53,108 --> 00:19:56,612
[tense music playing]

385
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:00,324
Ame?

386
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:02,576
[Audrey] What are you doing here?

387
00:20:03,785 --> 00:20:05,495
Are you with Atoy?

388
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:13,128
[Ame] Oh, no.

389
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:15,631
But I heard he's looking for you.

390
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:18,800
Audrey, please don't avoid Atoy.

391
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:23,222
Green shirt, smallest one.

392
00:20:23,722 --> 00:20:24,640
Martina?

393
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:26,850
Audrey.

394
00:20:27,517 --> 00:20:30,229
Why are you here? You know each other?

395
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:32,898
Yes, she's Ame.

396
00:20:32,981 --> 00:20:36,235
[in English] Uh, I'm just here to buy
coffee and some pastries for Janine.

397
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:39,446
So, Ame, are you alone?

398
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:43,408
Um, I'm with Ibyang.
She just went to the CR.

399
00:20:44,534 --> 00:20:47,412
[Audrey] Ibyang, Janine's schoolmate.

400
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:50,123
Atoy has been taking care of her
for a long time.

401
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:52,709
[in English] He even thought
of adopting her.

402
00:20:53,377 --> 00:20:56,004
Oh, it's fine that it didn't push through,

403
00:20:56,088 --> 00:21:00,092
because today we're meeting
the former head of the orphanage,

404
00:21:00,175 --> 00:21:01,301
Sister Norma.

405
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:04,680
She'll help us find Ibyang's parents.

406
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:06,515
Oh, really?

407
00:21:07,391 --> 00:21:08,934
[in English] Really?

408
00:21:09,017 --> 00:21:11,186
So, Ibyang grew up in the orphanage,

409
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:14,273
and she's going to meet
her real parents today?

410
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:15,857
[sighs]

411
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:18,694
Hi.

412
00:21:18,777 --> 00:21:21,113
[suspicious music playing]

413
00:21:21,196 --> 00:21:24,074
Why are you talking about me?

414
00:21:25,158 --> 00:21:26,535
Who are you?

415
00:21:27,327 --> 00:21:30,414
[in English] Hi! I'm Martina.
I'm Janine's aunt.

416
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:32,165
Why?

417
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:36,420
[in English] Um,
is something wrong, Martina?

418
00:21:36,503 --> 00:21:38,797
[in English] No. I'm just really happy

419
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,590
that she's gonna meet
her parents for the first time.

420
00:21:40,674 --> 00:21:43,593
[in English] I mean, you know me.
I love a family reunion story.

421
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:45,846
Doesn't seem like it.

422
00:21:45,929 --> 00:21:47,514
[sneaky music playing]

423
00:21:47,597 --> 00:21:49,933
Are you being fake with me?

424
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:53,228
[in English] Of course not! Oh my gosh.

425
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:55,147
[in English] You're so cute!

426
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:03,322
[music fades]

427
00:22:08,535 --> 00:22:09,828
[Ame] Oh, Miss Cita!

428
00:22:10,412 --> 00:22:11,997
You know, it's crazy!

429
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:13,915
Our meeting place was so far,

430
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:19,671
and Sister Norma didn't even show up.
Now, I can't contact them…

431
00:22:19,755 --> 00:22:22,632
[pensive music playing]

432
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:25,427
Miss Cita, are you okay?

433
00:22:26,928 --> 00:22:29,931
Just some new problems, Ame.

434
00:22:31,391 --> 00:22:34,227
Ah, do you want us to go to Atoy?

435
00:22:34,311 --> 00:22:36,646
So we can talk about your problem?

436
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:38,398
Ibyang is on her way to see him.

437
00:22:39,066 --> 00:22:41,485
[melodramatic music playing]

438
00:22:41,568 --> 00:22:42,986
No more…

439
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:45,447
I can't face him anymore.

440
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:48,033
[sobs]

441
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:50,994
Miss, why? Did something happen?

442
00:22:51,078 --> 00:22:56,124
[sobbing]

443
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:03,256
[Martina, in English] <i>Can you believe it?</i>

444
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:07,010
All this time, Audrey's real child
has been right around us.

445
00:23:08,011 --> 00:23:11,139
[in English] And the ironic part is
she's been living under Atoy's care.

446
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:14,017
[in English] Without him even knowing
that she's his real daughter.

447
00:23:14,101 --> 00:23:16,394
- [suspicious music playing]
- Are you sure?

448
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:17,771
[in English] Yes.

449
00:23:17,854 --> 00:23:22,484
And, hon, it's easy to follow
because they were meeting Sister Norma.

450
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:24,611
Ibyang is the child I gave her before.

451
00:23:24,694 --> 00:23:26,279
[smirks]

452
00:23:26,363 --> 00:23:27,948
[in English] I have
to give it to you, Martina.

453
00:23:29,116 --> 00:23:31,827
That's why you're my wife.
You act even while I'm resting.

454
00:23:32,410 --> 00:23:33,411
[in English] I know, right?

455
00:23:34,538 --> 00:23:35,831
But we need to plan this.

456
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:38,500
We need to get ahead of Atoy.

457
00:23:39,209 --> 00:23:41,711
It's risky. They're in the same house.

458
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:43,380
He must not know
that Ibyang is his daughter.

459
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:48,009
[tense music playing]

460
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:50,720
We waited for a long time.

461
00:23:50,804 --> 00:23:54,724
But Sister Norma didn't show up.

462
00:23:55,976 --> 00:24:00,188
So, we just bought food for you.

463
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:02,274
- [Atoy] Hmm.
- It's your favorite.

464
00:24:02,357 --> 00:24:04,359
Chicken feet, right?

465
00:24:05,610 --> 00:24:06,653
You knew that already.

466
00:24:11,658 --> 00:24:13,326
Ahh!

467
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:19,374
[pleasant music playing]

468
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:23,753
Oh, the chicken feet
walked straight into my mouth!

469
00:24:23,837 --> 00:24:26,256
[chuckles softly]

470
00:24:27,174 --> 00:24:30,886
You know, even if you're mischievous,

471
00:24:31,511 --> 00:24:35,932
I'm sure your parents will be happy
when they finally meet you.

472
00:24:37,684 --> 00:24:38,727
Oh my.

473
00:24:39,561 --> 00:24:42,731
That's what Ms. Martina said earlier too.

474
00:24:42,814 --> 00:24:43,899
[music fades]

475
00:24:43,982 --> 00:24:47,777
But the way she said it felt fake.

476
00:24:49,487 --> 00:24:50,530
- You know…
- Hmm?

477
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:52,657
Aunt Audrey was there too.

478
00:24:53,491 --> 00:24:54,951
She asked about you!

479
00:24:55,911 --> 00:24:58,705
Why don't you just talk to her

480
00:25:00,207 --> 00:25:02,042
and get back together?

481
00:25:05,420 --> 00:25:09,424
Ibyang, our situation is too complicated.

482
00:25:10,383 --> 00:25:11,301
I don't know.

483
00:25:12,052 --> 00:25:15,263
Looks like I'll really grow old single.

484
00:25:15,972 --> 00:25:17,557
Maybe that's my destiny.

485
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:23,230
I'm here anyway, Master.

486
00:25:24,522 --> 00:25:28,235
Even if my parents take me,

487
00:25:28,318 --> 00:25:30,153
I'll still come and visit you.

488
00:25:30,904 --> 00:25:31,947
[music fades]

489
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:37,160
So don't tear down my room upstairs, okay?

490
00:25:37,827 --> 00:25:42,207
[sentimental music playing]

491
00:25:42,290 --> 00:25:43,291
Ibyang.

492
00:25:45,627 --> 00:25:46,878
While…

493
00:25:47,963 --> 00:25:50,882
you haven't met your parents yet, can you…

494
00:25:51,591 --> 00:25:53,218
Can you stay here again?

495
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:56,680
Can you come back here?

496
00:25:58,223 --> 00:25:59,099
You and Ame.

497
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,227
Come back here first.

498
00:26:03,478 --> 00:26:04,479
Hmm.

499
00:26:05,897 --> 00:26:07,774
I'll think about it.

500
00:26:09,693 --> 00:26:10,694
Why?

501
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:13,238
Are you still mad at me?

502
00:26:13,321 --> 00:26:15,865
[pleasant music playing]

503
00:26:15,949 --> 00:26:17,450
Just kidding!

504
00:26:18,660 --> 00:26:20,996
Me? Mad at you?

505
00:26:21,079 --> 00:26:23,123
You're my Tatoy!

506
00:26:24,082 --> 00:26:25,500
That's forever.

507
00:26:26,626 --> 00:26:28,003
Really?

508
00:26:28,086 --> 00:26:29,296
- [Ibyang] Hmm.
- [chuckles softly]

509
00:26:31,339 --> 00:26:32,424
Oh?

510
00:26:33,508 --> 00:26:36,511
I thought these chicken feet were for me,
since it's my favorite,

511
00:26:36,594 --> 00:26:38,888
but it looks like they all walked
into your mouth.

512
00:26:38,972 --> 00:26:41,474
[chuckles]

513
00:26:41,558 --> 00:26:42,600
[Atoy] Huh?

514
00:26:42,684 --> 00:26:45,228
Chicken feet lover, huh.

515
00:26:45,312 --> 00:26:46,438
Want more?

516
00:26:46,521 --> 00:26:48,273
- Huh?
- Want more? Let's buy some.

517
00:26:48,356 --> 00:26:49,941
Okay.

518
00:26:50,025 --> 00:26:51,693
[music fades]

519
00:26:51,776 --> 00:26:53,695
[electronic blipping]

520
00:26:53,778 --> 00:26:57,490
[tense music playing]

521
00:27:01,911 --> 00:27:05,623
So we can bring her mother to you.

522
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:07,751
You'll bring her later?

523
00:27:07,834 --> 00:27:11,796
Honestly, I'm nervous
about this acting gig.

524
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:15,592
Because why won't they explain
why you need to get the child?

525
00:27:15,675 --> 00:27:17,552
I already spoke to Olga's friend.

526
00:27:17,635 --> 00:27:18,511
‪UP NEXT

527
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:19,888
They're with Atoy now.

528
00:27:19,971 --> 00:27:21,723
[Olga] There's a child here?

529
00:27:21,806 --> 00:27:23,141
Where is she?

530
00:27:23,224 --> 00:27:25,101
[Atoy] I thought you were here
for tailoring?

531
00:27:25,185 --> 00:27:26,019
Why are you looking for her?

532
00:27:26,102 --> 00:27:27,562
You're so grumpy.

533
00:27:27,645 --> 00:27:29,189
- ["Mr. Tailor" playing]
- [swooshes, then thuds]

534
00:27:29,272 --> 00:27:30,565
[Ame] Atoy!

535
00:27:30,648 --> 00:27:32,359
She's Ibyang's mother!

536
00:27:32,442 --> 00:27:33,651
[music swells]

537
00:27:33,735 --> 00:27:35,570
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

538
00:27:35,653 --> 00:27:37,655
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

539
00:27:37,739 --> 00:27:41,618
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

540
00:27:41,701 --> 00:27:43,036
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

541
00:27:43,119 --> 00:27:44,537
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
